{
  "about": "How a tool call's arguments are coerced (tools.py:113-127): both engines run every case, Python through tools.execute with the tool registered for the test, Rust through api::tools::normalize_with. A case gives the arguments sent and either what the tool receives or the refusal. A case with `intended` (an id of tests/rules/intended.toml) is the Rust engine's answer, which differs from Python's on purpose: only Rust runs it.",
